{"schema_version":1,"timestamp":"2026-11-03T09:39:22-05:00","cwd":"{NEBULA_PRODUCT_ROOT}","command":"python3 -c 'from pathlib import Path\nfrom datetime import datetime,timezone\nimport json\np=Path(\"/home/gajap/uSandbox/repos/nebula/nebula-insurance-brain/planning-mds/operations/evidence/runs/2026-11-02-5a00b0ff\")\nf=p/\"architect-implementation-review.md\";t=f.read_text()\nassert \"## Interpretation-Basis Decision\" not in t\nstamp=datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec=\"seconds\")\nt+=\"\"\"\n## Interpretation-Basis Decision \u2014 \"\"\"+stamp+\"\"\"\n\n**Decision:** Under the approved F0006 contract, INFERRED or AMBIGUOUS basis\nalone does not impose a mandatory human-review gate. Its basis remains visible\nand independent of confidence. A qualified typed source with no other\nrestriction can have `review_required=False`; that flag records the absence\nof F0006'\"'\"'s mandatory review reasons, not canonical approval or a new automatic\nacceptance policy.\n\nThe controlling sources are explicit:\n\n- [Master blueprint \u00a711](../../../../architecture/master-blueprint.md), line843:\n  \u201cgovernance policy decides whether review is required before canonicalization.\u201d\n  The preceding definition at lines784\u2013800 makes basis an epistemic dimension.\n- [Accepted ADR-0035, Decision](../../../../architecture/decisions/ADR-0035-interpretation-basis-is-first-class.md),\n  lines20\u201324: preserve EXPLICIT/INFERRED/AMBIGUOUS independently of fact mode.\n  This decision defines no basis-only mandatory-review rule.\n- [Approved assembly plan](../../../../features/F0006-assertion-plane-origin-and-interpretation-basis/feature-assembly-plan.md),\n  line272 assigns provenance hooks and existing confidence handling; the\n  eligibility row at line283 leaves qualified STATED/OCR/TRANSCRIBED claims to\n  existing policy and commit checks, with no new auto-acceptance. Line286\n  retains INFERRED/AMBIGUOUS without automatic acceptance. Lines288\u2013290 retain\n  the bounded guarded pilot commit and defer full orchestration.\n- [S0001 AC4](../../../../features/F0006-assertion-plane-origin-and-interpretation-basis/F0006-S0001-preserve-typed-source-claims.md),\n  line25 requires independent confidence/basis retention and forbids silent\n  conversion to EXPLICIT or automatic acceptance. Its entry contract at line34\n  explicitly grants assertion submission no canonical approval.\n- [PRD](../../../../features/F0006-assertion-plane-origin-and-interpretation-basis/PRD.md),\n  line20 requires zero canonical effects from assertion admission alone;\n  lines41\u201343 exclude full commit orchestration, automated deciders and new\n  grants. Line71 preserves basis independently of supplied confidence.\n- [Proposed ADR-0065](../../../../architecture/decisions/ADR-0065-assertion-admission-text-origin-and-mood.md),\n  lines71\u201384 specifies described-only and mood restrictions, not basis-only\n  mandatory review. [ADR-0075 \u00a73\u20134](../../../../architecture/decisions/ADR-0075-versioned-assertion-semantics-and-admission.md),\n  lines62\u201372 composes those restrictions, preserves correction basis and\n  requires separate current COMMIT/source READ authority in one unit of work.\n\nAccordingly, neither confidence0.99 nor a false `review_required` flag may\ncause canonical acceptance during admission or grant an automatic producer.\nAn explicit later commit proposal must independently satisfy fact-slot COMMIT,\ncurrent source READ, scope/proof/lineage and all kind/mood/evidence restrictions.\nSuch an authorized commit is a distinct governed mutation under the existing\npilot boundary; it is not evidence that admission auto-accepted the claim or\nthat a human reviewed it. The full policy/orchestration obligations remain\nwith their approved future owners. New consumers must not interpret this flag\nas authority to auto-accept.\n\nThe implementation preserves this distinction: the admission/writer path has\nzero canonical mutation calls; eligibility derives the specified mandatory\nrestrictions, while current commit runs separately through authorization and\nthe repository guard. No basis-only rule is added by this review. This is a\nconsistent reading of plan and story, so no plan-story reconciliation or\n`workstate.py decision --topic plan-story-reconcile` entry is warranted.\nThe parent is recording a focused behavior probe separately; this clarification\ndoes not claim an unobserved probe result.\n\"\"\"\nt=t.replace(\"line843\",\"line 843\").replace(\"lines784\",\"lines 784\").replace(\"lines20\",\"lines 20\").replace(\"line272\",\"line 272\").replace(\"line283\",\"line 283\").replace(\"Line286\",\"Line 286\").replace(\"Lines288\",\"Lines 288\").replace(\"line25\",\"line 25\").replace(\"line34\",\"line 34\").replace(\"line20\",\"line 20\").replace(\"lines41\",\"lines 41\").replace(\"Line71\",\"Line 71\").replace(\"lines71\",\"lines 71\").replace(\"lines62\",\"lines 62\").replace(\"confidence0.99\",\"confidence 0.99\")\nf.write_text(t)\nf=p/\"artifacts/test-results/architect-conformance-checks.json\";v=json.loads(f.read_text())\nv[\"interpretation_basis_decision\"]={\"reviewed_on\":stamp,\"basis_alone_requires_human_review\":False,\"admission_confers_canonical_approval\":False,\"explicit_commit_is_separate_governed_mutation\":True,\"plan_story_conflict\":False,\"source\":\"master-blueprint.md:843;ADR0035:20;approved plan:272,283,286;S0001AC4:25;PRD:20,41-43\",\"probe_result_claimed\":False}\nf.write_text(json.dumps(v,indent=2)+\"\\n\")\nprint(\"Architect interpretation appended with exact source/line citations; no source edits or workstate reconciliation.\")\n'","exit_code":0,"artifacts":[],"redactions":[]}
{"schema_version":1,"timestamp":"2026-11-03T09:39:30-05:00","cwd":"{NEBULA_PRODUCT_ROOT}","command":"python3 -c 'from pathlib import Path\nimport re\np=Path(\"/home/gajap/uSandbox/repos/nebula/nebula-insurance-brain/planning-mds/operations/evidence/runs/2026-11-02-5a00b0ff\")\nt=(p/\"architect-implementation-review.md\").read_text()\nfor path in re.findall(r\"\\]\\(([^)]+)\\)\",t):\n if not path.startswith((\"https:\",\"http:\")):assert (p/path).is_file(),path\nprint(\"All Architect report relative citations resolve; interpretation-basis decision recorded.\")\n'","exit_code":0,"artifacts":[],"redactions":[]}
