{"schema_version":1,"timestamp":"2026-11-03T21:39:42-05:00","cwd":"{NEBULA_PRODUCT_ROOT}","command":"python3 -c 'from pathlib import Path\np=Path('\"'\"'planning-mds/operations/evidence/runs/2026-11-02-5a00b0ff/security-review-report.md'\"'\"')\ns=p.read_text()\ns=s.replace('\"'\"'- Assessment: **PASS WITH RECOMMENDATIONS** for the bounded feature G3 review. This is not G4 approval, PM acceptance, a dependency waiver, production qualification, or producer activation.'\"'\"', '\"'\"'- Assessment: **PASS WITH RECOMMENDATIONS** for the bounded feature G3 review. G4 operator approval and named PM acceptance of the bounded dispositions were subsequently recorded at 2026-11-04T02:37:42.390119+00:00 in [gate-decisions.md](gate-decisions.md#g4-operator-approval-recorded); this does not resolve the technical findings or grant production qualification/producer activation.\\n- Disposition refresh: 2026-11-04 (UTC), after reading the actual approval record and passing G4 validation output.'\"'\"')\ns=s.replace('\"'\"'No unresolved implementation blocker remains in the reviewed source.'\"'\"', '\"'\"'No unresolved implementation blocker remains in the reviewed source. The four open recommendations are explicitly non-blocking/deferred for the accepted trusted local synthetic-fixture scope under the named PM dispositions below; SEC-05 still requires G7 reconciliation or a precise documented limitation before G8 closeout.'\"'\"')\ns=s.replace('\"'\"'Owner: AI Engineer + DevOps, with Security verification. Proposed target: 2026-11-10, and before production/untrusted shared conversion exposure. Tracking: SEC-01 in this report / proposed F0026 security carryover.'\"'\"', '\"'\"'Owner: AI Engineer + DevOps, with Security verification. Accepted follow-up target: 2026-11-10, and before untrusted or production PDF ingestion. Tracking: SEC-01 in this report; preproduction conversion-security carryover.'\"'\"')\ns=s.replace('\"'\"'Proposed bounded G4 mitigation: allow only the reviewed local synthetic-fixture feature acceptance; keep current pipeline/writer defaults, no new producer or public/untrusted deployment activation; treat ingestion/conversion dependency remediation and memory containment as explicit preconditions to broader production exposure. F0006 does not introduce or amplify the inherited route. This is a **proposal**, not PM/operator acceptance or a waiver.'\"'\"', '\"'\"'Accepted bounded G4 mitigation: **trusted local synthetic fixtures only**. Remediate/qualify affected conversion dependencies and verify memory/CPU/process isolation before untrusted or production PDF ingestion. Keep the reviewed pipeline/writer defaults and producer boundary. The operator explicitly approved the quoted mitigation; Codex / Product Manager recorded the named SEC-01 acceptance in [gate-decisions.md](gate-decisions.md#named-pm-recommendation-acceptances). SEC-01 remains an **open High technical finding**, deferred and non-blocking only within that accepted local scope. The acceptance is neither a remediation claim nor a dependency waiver or production activation.'\"'\"')\ns=s.replace('\"'\"'Owner: Security + Architect; proposed target 2026-11-10 / before production security qualification. Tracking: SEC-02. Proposed disposition is a bounded local feature carryover because these existing global documents are outside approved F0006 implementation scope; no passing audit or approval is fabricated.'\"'\"', '\"'\"'Owner: Security + Architect; accepted follow-up target 2026-11-10 / before production security qualification. Tracking: SEC-02. Codex / Product Manager explicitly accepted this non-blocking local feature carryover in [gate-decisions.md](gate-decisions.md#named-pm-recommendation-acceptances), because these existing global documents are outside approved F0006 implementation scope. The strict audit remains failed and the Medium finding remains open.'\"'\"')\ns=s.replace('\"'\"'Owner: Backend Developer + DevOps; proposed target 2026-11-17. Tracking: SEC-03. Proposed hardening carryover; not an authenticated DAST pass.'\"'\"', '\"'\"'Owner: Backend Developer + DevOps; accepted follow-up target 2026-11-17. Tracking: SEC-03. Codex / Product Manager accepted this non-blocking local feature hardening follow-up in [gate-decisions.md](gate-decisions.md#named-pm-recommendation-acceptances). The Low finding remains open; the anonymous DAST limitation remains unchanged.'\"'\"')\ns=s.replace('\"'\"'Owner: Architect; target G7 before closeout. Tracking: SEC-05. This is a coverage-map finding, not evidence those routes omit authorization.'\"'\"', '\"'\"'Owner: Architect; accepted follow-up target G7 before G8 closeout. Tracking: SEC-05. Codex / Product Manager accepted this non-blocking feature follow-up in [gate-decisions.md](gate-decisions.md#named-pm-recommendation-acceptances), with mandatory G7 reconciliation or a precise source-backed static-analysis limitation before closeout. The Low coverage-map finding remains open until that evidence exists; no missing runtime authorization is inferred.'\"'\"')\nstart=s.index('\"'\"'## Recommendation Disposition'\"'\"')\nend=s.index('\"'\"'## Per-Story Security Assessment'\"'\"',start)\ns=s[:start]+'\"'\"''\"'\"''\"'\"'## Recommendation Disposition\n\nThese are **accepted, non-blocking/deferred recommendations only for the trusted local synthetic-fixture feature scope**. Their original severities are retained. Each has an owner, follow-up and named PM acceptance in the actual [G4 record](gate-decisions.md#g4-operator-approval-recorded). No technical finding is silently converted to resolved.\n\n- [high] SEC-01: accepted bounded mitigation restricts feature use to trusted local synthetic fixtures; qualify/remediate affected conversion dependencies and verify memory/CPU/process isolation before untrusted or production PDF ingestion; target 2026-11-10; PM acceptance: Codex / Product Manager, gate-decisions.md, Named PM Recommendation Acceptances \u2014 owner: AI Engineer + DevOps (Securi